# Generated from: specs/194-move-start-and-execute-orchestration-into-controllers-behind-sibling-workers/requirements.md
Feature: Move start and execute orchestration into controllers behind sibling workers
  As a Herdr OMP execute operator
  I want start-issue and execute orchestration to run as deterministic Node controllers invoked by compact prompts
  So that the model is not parsing Herdr JSON, fenced shell, and handoff schemas on every issue

  # --- Happy Path ---

  @SCN001
  Scenario: start controller preserves every current start outcome
    Given a sibling start worker with "$ARGUMENTS: #N"
    When it runs the compact start workflow
    Then it invokes node scripts/start-issue.mjs --issue N
    And that controller performs parse, gh issue view, slug, parseBodyRelationships dependency re-proof, dirty-tree, default-branch resolution, gh issue develop, and best-effort Project In Progress
    And it writes .omp/sdlc/handoffs/N-start.json
    And it prints "NMG_SDLC_HANDOFF: .omp/sdlc/handoffs/N-start.json"
    And execute does not call startIssue() itself
    And failed handoffs use reasonCode values no_issue_number, issue_unreadable, dependency_unreadable, dependency_blocked, dirty_tree, default_branch_unreadable, branch_checkout_failed with intervention true and step start
    And leftover spike labels do not skip implement/verify
    And Project status mutation failure does not fail the handoff

  @SCN002
  Scenario: execute controller preserves the current queue
    Given /sdlc-execute [#N ...] in a Herdr OMP session
    When the file command expands
    Then the compact execute workflow requires HERDR_ENV=1 plus HERDR_SOCKET_PATH and HERDR_PANE_ID
    And it runs node scripts/sdlc-execute.mjs run with the trimmed arguments and passes output through
    And run owns preflight, backlog/args, unapproved-spec stop, run.json, pane split, worker launch, stall recovery, handoff validate, close-vs-keep, resume, notification, default-branch sync, and post-MERGED+CLOSED local branch delete
    And the default blocking worker wait is not overridden by a shorter timeout and tolerates at least one hour of active issue execution
    And existing helper CLIs still work
    And src/extension.ts still does not register /sdlc-execute
    And invalid args print "Usage: /sdlc-execute [#N ...]" and stop non-zero
    And missing omp integration prints exactly "Run: herdr integration install omp" and stops with no mutations

  # --- Alternative Paths ---

  @SCN003
  Scenario: four sibling workers remain
    Given issue N with an approved spec
    When run executes the pipeline
    Then it still launches s<N>-start, s<N>-implement, s<N>-verify, and s<N>-deliver as --kind omp workers
    And workerPrompt still inlines the compact start workflow rather than executing start in-process
    And implement still inlines write-code + simplify
    And deliver still inlines open-pr + address-pr-comments
    And a failed or intervention true handoff keeps that pane and stops the queue
    And the execute pane never edits product code, never implements tasks, and never opens PRs

  @SCN004
  Scenario: compact prompts do not drop documented Herdr behavior
    Given the execute controller
    When it splits and launches
    Then it still uses herdr pane layout, herdr pane split --current --direction <right|down> --cwd "$PWD" --no-focus, herdr agent start s<N>-<step> --kind omp --pane <id>, and herdr agent prompt --wait
    And it closes only panes this run created
    And it notifies with herdr notification show "nmg-sdlc stopped" --body "Stopped on #<N> <step>. Worker pane <pane_id> agent s<N>-<step> left open." --sound request
    And split direction is right when width >= height else down, missing dimension down
    And agent names match ^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,31}$, never sdlc- prefix, never --kind pi, never herdr server stop

  # --- Error Handling ---

  @SCN005
  Scenario: start and execute fail closed on missing preconditions
    Given start CLI has no valid --issue
    When node scripts/start-issue.mjs runs
    Then it exits 2, prints "Usage: node scripts/start-issue.mjs --issue N", and writes no handoff
    And runExecute with HERDR_ENV unset prints that execute requires a Herdr OMP session and starts no workers
    And a blocked Depends-on parent writes reasonCode dependency_blocked before gh issue develop
